Module 7: FPGA to STM32 Interface (FSMC memory-mapped)

Purpose:
- Provide a high-throughput interface for STM32 to read captured frames and control FPGA registers.

Schematic/Interface description:
- Expose FPGA logic or external SRAM as a memory region on FSMC bank 1 (16-bit data bus).
- Signals:
  - DATA[15:0] <-> FSMC D0..D15
  - ADDR[0..n] <-> FSMC A0..An (mapped to FPGA register map)
  - CS_N, RD_N, WR_N <-> FSMC control signals
  - IRQ_N from FPGA -> STM32 EXTI line
- Registers: CONTROL (arm, stop), STATUS (ready, overflow), PRE_SAMPLES, POST_SAMPLES, DECIMATE_FACTOR

Software:
- STM32 uses DMA to burst-read frame buffer from FSMC into RAM; double-buffering to allow UI update while next frame captured.

Verification:
- Validate read/write transactions, confirm IRQ triggers on capture complete, measure read throughput via DMA.
